# Power workstream (work/power/power.md job 1a). Raises the wheel/input
# timer period from 400 us to 1000 us, the Neo equivalent of nanitecfw's
# wheel-poll change in power_idle.patch. Module 1 key init is the ONLY
# caller of TimerPeriodSet 0x030510A2 in the whole image (callsites sweep
# over all 82 modules), so this one immediate is the single funnel for
# the wheel sampling rate: IRQ 19 (exception 0x23) -> handler 0x03061ACC
# -> ack Timer0 -> tail-call wheel quadrature decoder 0x03061936.
# Keys are NOT sampled by this timer (the input task 0x03061AB2 is a
# SysTick callback, Reload=2 ticks), so key latency is unchanged; the
# cost is wheel-step detection latency, worst case +1.2 ms (power.md).
name: power-wheel-period-1000us
kind: module
module: 1
region: code
address: 0x307d2d6
gate: build refuses unless the 4 stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: TimerPeriodSet(0, usTick=400, nsTick) at module 1 exec
  0x0307D2DE; the usTick low word is loaded by the mov.w at 0x0307D2D6
  (r3 = 0 is the high word, set at 0x0307D2D4). Changing only the low
  word 400 -> 1000 raises the Timer0 period to 1000 us. Cuts wheel IRQ
  wakes from 2500/s to 1000/s. Data-only edit (one immediate); reversible
  by rebuilding from stock without this patch.
expect: 4ff4c872
replace: 4ff47a72
